( '6.1', 'CASE 6.1.044', 'Vehicles as Fixed or Resale Assets', 'Analyze how a franchise licence held for long-term use is classified as an intangible non-current asset. Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['A patent counts as a current asset whenever its value is difficult to estimate precisely.', 'A trademark registration lacks physical substance but is classified as a non-current intangible asset because it provides expected long-term benefit.', 'Although a trademark registration cannot be touched, it appears among non-current assets rather than current assets because of its long-term value.', 'A trademark is excluded from non-current assets because it has no physical substance.', 'A trademark registration is recorded as an intangible non-current asset alongside tangible assets such as buildings and machinery.'], ARRAY[false, true, true, false, true], ARRAY['FALSE — Valuation difficulty does not reclassify a patent; expected long-term benefit keeps it a non-current intangible asset.', 'TRUE — Long-term expected benefit, not physical form, justifies the non-current classification of a trademark registration.', 'TRUE — Long-term value places an intangible trademark registration among non-current rather than current assets.', 'FALSE — Physical substance is not required for non-current classification; a trademark qualifies through its long-term value.', 'TRUE — Intangible and tangible non-current assets, including a trademark registration, sit together in the same balance sheet section.'], '3/5', 44, 'full' ),
( '6.1', 'CASE 6.1.045', 'Forklifts in Fixed Versus Current Assets', 'Review how an import licence held for ongoing trading rights is classified on the balance sheet. Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['A trademark is classified as a current asset because it is intangible and therefore easily converted into cash within a year.', 'The absence of physical form does not prevent a trademark registration from being classified as a non-current asset.', 'A trademark registration purchased to protect or exploit a business''s operations over several years is grouped with intangible non-current assets.', 'Because a trademark cannot be touched, it is recorded as an expense rather than as an asset on the balance sheet.', 'A trademark registration is not classified as a current asset because it is not expected to be converted into cash within the normal operating cycle.'], ARRAY[false, true, true, false, true], ARRAY['FALSE — A trademark is a non-current intangible asset because it provides benefit over several years, not because it converts to cash quickly.', 'TRUE — Physical form is not a requirement for non-current classification of a trademark registration.', 'TRUE — Multi-year protective or exploitative value groups a trademark registration with intangible non-current assets.', 'FALSE — A trademark with expected long-term benefit is recorded as an intangible non-current asset, not expensed immediately.', 'TRUE — Because a trademark registration is not expected to convert into cash within the operating cycle, it is excluded from current assets.'], '3/5', 45, 'full' ),
( '6.1', 'CASE 6.1.046', 'Ovens Held for Use or Sale', 'Analyze how a distribution licence supporting long-term operations is classified as an intangible asset. Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['Non-current assets can never include a trademark because that section is reserved strictly for tangible items like machinery.', 'A trademark is treated as inventory because it is intended for use rather than for physical display.', 'A trademark loses its non-current classification as soon as the business begins actively using it.', 'A business holding a trademark registration for continued exclusive use records it as an intangible non-current asset rather than as inventory.', 'A copyright lacks physical substance but is classified as a non-current intangible asset because it provides expected long-term benefit.'], ARRAY[false, false, false, true, true], ARRAY['FALSE — The non-current assets section includes intangible items such as a trademark alongside tangible assets.', 'FALSE — Long-term exclusive use, not physical display, places a trademark among non-current intangible assets, not inventory.', 'FALSE — Active use does not remove a trademark''s non-current classification; it confirms the long-term benefit that justifies it.', 'TRUE — Continued exclusive use, not resale intent, keeps a trademark registration out of inventory and within intangible non-current assets.', 'TRUE — Long-term expected benefit, not physical form, justifies the non-current classification of a copyright.'], '5/5', 46, 'full' ),
( '6.1', 'CASE 6.1.047', 'Sewing Machines and Asset Classification', 'Consider a farm business that owns tractors for cultivation while holding harvested grain in storage awaiting sale. Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['Although a copyright cannot be touched, it appears among non-current assets rather than current assets because of its long-term value.', 'A copyright is recorded as an intangible non-current asset alongside tangible assets such as buildings and machinery.', 'The absence of physical form does not prevent a copyright from being classified as a non-current asset.', 'A copyright purchased to protect or exploit a business''s operations over several years is grouped with intangible non-current assets.', 'A copyright is not classified as a current asset because it is not expected to be converted into cash within the normal operating cycle.'], ARRAY[true, true, true, true, true], ARRAY['TRUE — Long-term value places an intangible copyright among non-current rather than current assets.', 'TRUE — Intangible and tangible non-current assets, including a copyright, sit together in the same balance sheet section.', 'TRUE — Physical form is not a requirement for non-current classification of a copyright.', 'TRUE — Multi-year protective or exploitative value groups a copyright with intangible non-current assets.', 'TRUE — Because a copyright is not expected to convert into cash within the operating cycle, it is excluded from current assets.'], '5/5', 47, 'full' ),
( '6.1', 'CASE 6.1.048', 'Generators as Operating Equipment', 'Analyze how copyright protection is classified as an intangible non-current asset. Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['A business holding a copyright for continued exclusive use records it as an intangible non-current asset rather than as inventory.', 'A customer list acquired in a takeover lacks physical substance but is classified as a non-current intangible asset because it provides expected long-term benefit.', 'Although a customer list acquired in a takeover cannot be touched, it appears among non-current assets rather than current assets because of its long-term value.', 'A trademark counts as a current asset whenever its value is difficult to estimate precisely.', 'A brand licence is excluded from non-current assets because it has no physical substance.'], ARRAY[true, true, true, false, false], ARRAY['TRUE — Continued exclusive use, not resale intent, keeps a copyright out of inventory and within intangible non-current assets.', 'TRUE — Long-term expected benefit, not physical form, justifies the non-current classification of a customer list acquired in a takeover.', 'TRUE — Long-term value places an intangible customer list acquired in a takeover among non-current rather than current assets.', 'FALSE — Valuation difficulty does not reclassify a trademark; expected long-term benefit keeps it a non-current intangible asset.', 'FALSE — Physical substance is not required for non-current classification; a brand licence qualifies through its long-term value.'], '3/5', 48, 'full' ),
( '6.1', 'CASE 6.1.049', 'Tractors in Farm Business Balance Sheets', 'Review how a software licence used over several years is classified as a non-current asset. Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['A brand licence is classified as a current asset because it is intangible and therefore easily converted into cash within a year.', 'A customer list acquired in a takeover is recorded as an intangible non-current asset alongside tangible assets such as buildings and machinery.', 'Because a brand licence cannot be touched, it is recorded as an expense rather than as an asset on the balance sheet.', 'Non-current assets can never include a brand licence because that section is reserved strictly for tangible items like machinery.', 'A brand licence is treated as inventory because it is intended for use rather than for physical display.'], ARRAY[false, true, false, false, false], ARRAY['FALSE — A brand licence is a non-current intangible asset because it provides benefit over several years, not because it converts to cash quickly.', 'TRUE — Intangible and tangible non-current assets, including a customer list acquired in a takeover, sit together in the same balance sheet section.', 'FALSE — A brand licence with expected long-term benefit is recorded as an intangible non-current asset, not expensed immediately.', 'FALSE — The non-current assets section includes intangible items such as a brand licence alongside tangible assets.', 'FALSE — Long-term exclusive use, not physical display, places a brand licence among non-current intangible assets, not inventory.'], '5/5', 49, 'full' ),
( '6.1', 'CASE 6.1.050', 'Server Racks as Fixed Assets', 'Analyze how a mortgage on business premises is classified as a non-current liability. Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['The absence of physical form does not prevent a customer list acquired in a takeover from being classified as a non-current asset.', 'A customer list acquired in a takeover purchased to protect or exploit a business''s operations over several years is grouped with intangible non-current assets.', 'A customer list acquired in a takeover is not classified as a current asset because it is not expected to be converted into cash within the normal operating cycle.', 'A business holding a customer list acquired in a takeover for continued exclusive use records it as an intangible non-current asset rather than as inventory.', 'A brand licence loses its non-current classification as soon as the business begins actively using it.'], ARRAY[true, true, true, true, false], ARRAY['TRUE — Physical form is not a requirement for non-current classification of a customer list acquired in a takeover.', 'TRUE — Multi-year protective or exploitative value groups a customer list acquired in a takeover with intangible non-current assets.', 'TRUE — Because a customer list acquired in a takeover is not expected to convert into cash within the operating cycle, it is excluded from current assets.', 'TRUE — Continued exclusive use, not resale intent, keeps a customer list acquired in a takeover out of inventory and within intangible non-current assets.', 'FALSE — Active use does not remove a brand licence''s non-current classification; it confirms the long-term benefit that justifies it.'], '5/5', 50, 'full' ),
