Evaluate the following economic assertions:', ARRAY['Cash flow from operating activities rose from €124 thousand in Year 1 to €146 thousand in Year 2, an increase of more than 10%.', 'In Year 2, operating cash flow of €146 thousand was lower than operating cash flow before working capital changes of €236 thousand.', 'Because investing cash flow was €-232 thousand in Year 2, the business must be in financial difficulty.', 'In Year 1, operating cash flow of €124 thousand was lower than operating cash flow before working capital changes of €194 thousand.', 'Cash flow from investing activities was €-115 thousand in Year 1 and €-232 thousand in Year 2, both negative on this extract.'], ARRAY[true, true, false, true, true], ARRAY['TRUE — Operating growth about 17.7%.', 'TRUE — Operating cash was below the pre-working-capital figure in Year 2.', 'FALSE — Negative investing often reflects asset purchases.', 'TRUE — The same pattern held in Year 1.', 'TRUE — Investing outflows were negative in both years.'], '2/5', 123, 'full' ),
